---
import Profile from '../../layouts/Profile.astro';
import { fixtures } from '../../lib/workflow-lesson';
---

<Profile
  title="How do you know an AI update worked? — Dave Bettner"
  description="Try a small inventory example to see how source checks, approval, and application readback make an AI-assisted update verifiable."
  page="fit"
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap">
    <h1>How do you know an AI update worked?</h1>
    <p class="lead">A convincing proposal is a starting point. Before trusting an update, check its source, approve the change, and read the result from the application.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a href="/ai-workflows/">How I build AI workflows</a></div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap lesson prose">
    <section aria-labelledby="lesson-heading">
      <h2 id="lesson-heading">Three different kinds of evidence.</h2>
      <ol class="lesson-steps">
        <li><strong>A proposal.</strong> An assistant suggests a new value. Check that its source is current and its calculation is right before allowing a write.</li>
        <li><strong>A write receipt.</strong> An application reports that it accepted the change. That tells you about the request, but you still need to inspect the saved result.</li>
        <li><strong>A checked final state.</strong> Read the application again and compare its saved value and revision with the approved update.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>If a response gets lost, the write may already have succeeded. Read the application before deciding to retry. Otherwise, you risk applying the same change twice.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="workflow-demo" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
      <h2 id="example-heading">Try it with an inventory update.</h2>
      <p>A shop starts with 100 units, receives 30, and ships 20. The expected stock is <strong>110 units</strong>. Try the valid proposal, then see what changes when the source is stale, the calculation is wrong, or a write response is lost.</p>
      <p class="scope-note">This example uses fictional inventory data and deterministic local checks. No AI model or external application is called. State stays in this page and resets when you reload.</p>

      <div class="fixture-control">
        <label for="fixture">Try a case</label>
        <select id="fixture" disabled>
          {fixtures.map(fixture => <option value={fixture.id}>{fixture.label}</option>)}
        </select>
        <button id="reset-example" class="lesson-button" type="button" disabled>Reset example</button>
      </div>

      <div class="records">
        <table>
          <caption>Source records</caption>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Source revision</th><td id="source-revision">inventory-7</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Proposal inspected</th><td id="inspected-revision">inventory-7</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Starting stock</th><td>100 units</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Received</th><td>30 units</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Shipped</th><td>20 units</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <table>
          <caption>Proposal and application</caption>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Proposed stock</th><td id="proposed-stock">110 units</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Application stock</th><td id="application-stock">100 units</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Application revision</th><td id="application-revision">3</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Writes made</th><td id="write-count">0</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Write receipt</th><td id="write-receipt">Not requested</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="read-note">Application values show the last read. Applying a change does not refresh them. Use “Read application” to inspect the saved result.</p>

      <div class="demo-actions">
        <button id="check-proposal" class="lesson-button" type="button" disabled>Check proposal</button>
        <button id="apply-proposal" class="button" type="button" disabled>Approve and apply</button>
        <button id="read-application" class="lesson-button" type="button" disabled>Read application</button>
      </div>
      <p id="workflow-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Enable JavaScript to try the controls. The example above shows the source and proposed update.</p>
      <noscript><p>The lesson and static example are available without JavaScript. The controls need JavaScript because they update a local application record in your browser.</p></noscript>
      <ul id="proposal-checks" aria-label="Proposal check results" hidden></ul>

      <h3 class="log-heading">What happened</h3>
      <ol id="workflow-log"><li>No interactive actions have run.</li></ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="takeaway-heading">
      <h2 id="takeaway-heading">Make the result easy to inspect.</h2>
      <p>The same questions apply when an assistant updates a report, a customer record, or a project. Which source did it inspect? What exactly did you approve? What is saved now? A useful workflow makes those answers available to the person responsible for the result.</p>
      <p>I use this approach in my <a href="/ai-workflows/">AI workflow work</a>. You can also inspect the <a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/">Accounting Acceptance Lab</a> or try <a href="/work/krowbar/">Krowbar’s fictional reporting demo</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Profile>

<script>
  import { advanceWorkflow, createWorkflow, fixtures, type WorkflowAction } from '../../lib/workflow-lesson';

  const demo = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#workflow-demo')!;
  const select = demo.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#fixture')!;
  const reset = demo.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#reset-example')!;
  const check = demo.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#check-proposal')!;
  const apply = demo.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#apply-proposal')!;
  const read = demo.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#read-application')!;
  const status = demo.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#workflow-status')!;
  const checks = demo.querySelector<HTMLUListElement>('#proposal-checks')!;
  const log = demo.querySelector<HTMLOListElement>('#workflow-log')!;
  let state = createWorkflow('valid');

  function render() {
    const values = {
      'source-revision': state.source.revision,
      'inspected-revision': state.inspectedSourceRevision,
      'proposed-stock': `${state.candidateStockBalance} units`,
      'application-stock': `${state.lastReadApplication.stockBalance} units`,
      'application-revision': String(state.lastReadApplication.revision),
      'write-count': String(state.writeCount),
      'write-receipt': { 'not-requested': 'Not requested', accepted: 'Accepted', 'response-lost': 'Response lost' }[state.receiptStatus],
    };
    for (const [id, value] of Object.entries(values)) demo.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`#${id}`)!.textContent = value;
    status.textContent = state.message;
    checks.hidden = state.checks.length === 0;
    checks.replaceChildren(...state.checks.map(result => {
      const item = document.createElement('li');
      item.textContent = `${result.passes ? 'Pass' : 'Fail'}. ${result.explanation}`;
      return item;
    }));
    log.replaceChildren(...state.log.map(message => {
      const item = document.createElement('li');
      item.textContent = message;
      return item;
    }));
    check.disabled = state.phase !== 'proposal' && state.phase !== 'blocked';
    apply.disabled = state.phase !== 'checked';
    read.disabled = false;
    reset.disabled = false;
    select.disabled = false;
  }

  function run(action: WorkflowAction) {
    state = advanceWorkflow(state, action);
    render();
  }

  select.addEventListener('change', () => {
    const fixture = fixtures.find(fixture => fixture.id === select.value);
    if (!fixture) return;
    state = createWorkflow(fixture.id);
    render();
  });
  reset.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state = createWorkflow(state.fixture);
    render();
  });
  check.addEventListener('click', () => run('check'));
  apply.addEventListener('click', () => run('apply'));
  read.addEventListener('click', () => run('read'));
  render();
</script>

<style>
  .lesson { max-width: 800px; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .lesson-steps { padding-left: 24px; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .lesson p + p { margin-top: 16px; }
  .scope-note, .read-note { color: var(--secondary); font-size: 14px; }
  .fixture-control { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-block: 28px; }
  .fixture-control label { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }
  select, button { font: inherit; }
  select { max-width: 100%; min-height: 49px; padding: 10px 32px 10px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--secondary); border-radius: var(--radius-control); background: var(--page); color: var(--text); font-size: 14px; }
  .lesson-button { min-height: 49px; padding: 12px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--secondary); border-radius: var(--radius-control); background: var(--page); color: var(--text); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
  button { cursor: pointer; }
  button:disabled, select:disabled { color: var(--secondary); background: var(--surface-raised); border-color: var(--border); cursor: default; transform: none; }
  .records { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 36px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed; font-size: 14px; }
  caption { text-align: left; padding-bottom: 12px; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; }
  th, td { padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  th { width: 59%; padding-right: 12px; text-align: left; font-weight: 500; }
  td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .read-note { margin-top: 16px; }
  .demo-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-block: 24px 20px; }
  #workflow-status { font-weight: 600; }
  #proposal-checks { margin-block: 20px; padding-left: 24px; }
  .log-heading { margin-top: 28px; font-size: 19px; }
  #workflow-log { padding-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 14px; }
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .lesson-button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--surface-raised); }
    .button:hover:disabled { color: var(--secondary); background: var(--surface-raised); border-color: var(--border); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .records { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .fixture-control { align-items: stretch; }
    .fixture-control label { width: 100%; }
    .fixture-control select { flex: 1 1 100%; }
    .demo-actions { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
  }
</style>
